      "summaries": {
        "en": "Hysteria is a proxy tool designed to bypass network censorship while delivering high-speed connections. It uses a custom protocol built on QUIC, which optimizes data transmission over unreliable or throttled networks by aggressively controlling packet loss and congestion. This makes it ideal for users in restrictive regions or those needing fast, stable access to blocked content. You can deploy it as a SOCKS5 or HTTP proxy, or even set up a VPN-like TUN interface. Its resilience against deep packet inspection and performance under high latency make it a practical choice for circumvention.",
        "zh": "Hysteria 是一个专为突破网络审查而设计的代理工具，同时提供极快的连接速度。它的核心技术是建立在 QUIC 协议之上的自定义协议，通过激进地控制丢包和拥塞，在不稳定或限速的网络环境下优化数据传输。这使其特别适合在限制严格的地区使用，或需要快速稳定访问被屏蔽内容的场景。你可以将其部署为 SOCKS5 或 HTTP 代理，甚至配置成类似 VPN 的 TUN 接口。它能够有效抵抗深度包检测，并在高延迟下保持性能，是网络穿透的实用选择。",
        "es": "Hysteria is a proxy tool designed to bypass network censorship while delivering high-speed connections. It uses a custom protocol built on QUIC, which optimizes data transmission over unreliable or throttled networks by aggressively controlling packet loss and congestion. This makes it ideal for users in restrictive regions or those needing fast, stable access to blocked content. You can deploy it as a SOCKS5 or HTTP proxy, or even set up a VPN-like TUN interface. Its resilience against deep packet inspection and performance under high latency make it a practical choice for circumvention.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "hysteria stands out for censorship-circumvention, golang, and http-proxy in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Hysteria is a proxy tool designed to bypass network censorship while delivering high-speed connections. It uses a custom protocol built on QUIC, which optimizes data transmission over unreliable or throttled networks by aggressively controlling packet loss and congestion. This makes it ideal for users in restrictive regions or those needing fast, stable access to blocked content. You can deploy it as a SOCKS5 or HTTP proxy, or even set up a VPN-like TUN interface. Its resilience against deep packet inspection and performance under high latency make it a practical choice for circumvention.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/apernet/hysteria for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
